<?php
/**
 * readme_row.php - stage the README.md row for the Help Center v2 tree.
 *
 *   php readme_row.php --stage <stage dir>
 *
 * Inserts one row into section 2's "Area | Files" table, right before the
 * "| Preset engine |" row, keeping the file's own line endings. Idempotent.
 */
$opts = getopt('', array('stage:'));
if (empty($opts['stage'])) { fwrite(STDERR, "usage: --stage <dir>\n"); exit(2); }
$path = rtrim($opts['stage'], '/\\') . '/README.md';
$s = file_get_contents($path);
if ($s === false) { fwrite(STDERR, "cannot read $path\n"); exit(2); }
$eol = (strpos($s, "\r\n") !== false) ? "\r\n" : "\n";
$row = '| Help Center v2 (phases 0-6 deployed 2026-10-15; switched ON 2026-10-15 15:59; the v1 body removed 2026-10-19) | `help/manifest.php` - the audience gate (`pnb_help_show()`: viewer / writer / admin; built, OFF until a `help/gate.on` marker or `PNB_HELP_GATE`), and the registry (categories a reader arrives with; per topic id, title, audience, aliases, keywords, `extra` = fragments folded into the topic: the Scheduler shows Dynamic Values, Skip When, Search Filter and On Completion as one book, Security shows the Access List); `help/loader.php` assembles `help/topics/<id>.php` (32: the SQL Editor split into SQL Editor, Query Prompts, Importing External Files, Cross-Database Subqueries) + `help/tips/<id>.php` (5) in manifest order. `help_content.php` and `help_manifest.php` keep their URLs as shims that hand over to the fragments (since 2026-10-19 the shims are all they are: the 12,000-line v1 body, the `help/v2.on` switch and the admin preview cookie are gone, `pnb_help_v2_active()` always answers true, and the v1 file is in git history up to bcbf7da), so index.php and the dashboard are unchanged; `js/main.js` gained one behaviour (2026-10-14): a jump link or `?` icon whose anchor lives in another topic activates that topic (`activateHelpTopic` re-resolves the owner; a folded topic opened without an anchor lands on its own start), so cross-references between topics work. Duplicated passages are collapsed to ONE canonical section (`data-canonical="key"` on its heading) and pointers (`data-canonical-ref="key"` on a `data-jump-to` link): dynamic dates, me() values, access-list entries, scheduled-snapshot rotation, quick-open shortcuts, template placeholders. Two engines are deliberately kept apart and cross-linked, not merged: the SQL and snippet `me()` key tables, and the browser vs scheduler search grammars. `help_retrieval.php` builds the AI help chunks from the fragments into `cache/help_chunks.json` (the one cache since 2026-10-19, VER 7; signature = count + newest mtime + total size; every chunk carries its audience; prebuilt on live by `penumbra_tests\\helpv2\\prebuild_caches.php` because the web tier cannot write `cache/`). Topic ids, anchor ids and `data-tip` keys are a contract (42 `?` icons, `#help=` links, 40+ suites): a renamed topic lists its old id in `aliases`, which ride in `data-extra`. Phase 2 (2026-10-15) rewrote the twelve viewer topics to the tier standard (Search, Grouping, Column Summaries, Pivot, Visualization, Snapshots, Journal, Download, Copy, Email, Settings, Dashboards): one `?` per feature with an "Open it:" line and a jump row, parameter tables with examples, paragraphs under 80 words, no emoji headings, no em-dashes; every code example, key and number of the old text survives (equivalence P9, with deliberate drops listed in `pnb_help_v2_dropped_tokens()`), the Email help\'s stale 2,000-row embed gate became the relay cap (main.js `ROW_EMBED_CEILING` = 25,000 since 2026-08-30) and the theme list gained Monochrome. Phase 3 (2026-10-15) did the same for the writer and administrator topics (SQL Editor, Query Prompts, Importing External Files, Cross-Database Subqueries, Saving a Report, Save Preferences, Security and Access List, Version History, View Options, Power Features, the Scheduler book, Report Repository, Auditor): the settings every scheduled task shares left the Email section for sections of their own, the Scheduler\'s and the Auditor\'s flex-div lists became tables with one aspect per row, the shortcut tables live only in Power Features, and the prompt "reserved names" rule moved from the SQL Editor to Query Prompts; the Custom Code reference is phase 4 (2026-10-15): ONE registry, `help/snippets.php` (41 entries: signature, a parameter table with an example per parameter, forms, body, related), renders `help/topics/optionsHelpLightbox.php` through `tests/gen_snippets_help.php`; the topic header carries the registry\'s sha256 and lint L17 fails while it is stale, L18 keeps the registry\'s names equal to the editor\'s `PENUMBRA_SNIPPET_FN_NAMES`. Phase 4b turned every flex-div pseudo-table in the Custom Code bodies into a real table, one aspect per row (lint L19), and phase 5 settled every coverage-map gap: `dsearch`, `eview`, `calc` and `embed` in Power Features, the pivot share types named as the builder shows them, the Prompt Generator and Tag Generator controls, the scheduler\'s Private Key (PEM) and Reason for override fields; `ai_system_prompt.php` is staged with an `avg()` heading (its deploy = run `renew_ai_cache.php`). Phase 6 (2026-10-15) added the Ask page (topic `askHelpLightbox`, endpoint `help_ask.php`, library `help/ask.php`, client `js/penumbra_help_ask.js`): a question answered from the help passages alone (retrieval restricted to the reader\'s audience), cached as a card others can vote on, behind a per-person minute limit and a shared day budget; a viewer asking about a writer or administrator feature is told first to ask the report owner (or an administrator) to set it up; retrieval runs in a recall mode for the page, so a one-word question such as "how do I hide a column" finds the Columns section; every claim in the help was traced to the live code on 2026-10-15 (2,213 claims; 54 wrong and 130 partial statements corrected across 29 topics, three tip stores and the Custom Code registry; report: penumbra_tests\\helpv2\\ACCURACY_REPORT_2026-10-15.md); switches `help/ask.off`, `help/ask.writer`, `help/ask.admin`; state beside the maintenance state; `help_retrieval.php` VER 5 (chunks carry their topic id, `pnb_help_retrieve_chunks()`). Table cells carry an inline `white-space: normal` and the topic header a panel-safe sticky style, because the dashboard\'s own help panel strips the `.lightbox-content` wrapper that neutralises main.css\'s report-table rules. Rollback of the v1 removal = `git revert` of its commit. Suite `penumbra_tests\\helpv2` (lint L1-L20, the audience-gate matrix E0/E1c/E3-E6 (E7 and the v1 comparison P1-P9 retired with the v1 body), retrieval R1/R3/R4/R6-R10, headless jump harness J1-J2, visual harness, coverage map, Ask tests A1-A10 + a headless client harness, 25 mutants). |';
if (preg_match('/^\| Help Center v2 [^\n]*\|\r?$/m', $s, $m)) {
    if (trim($m[0]) === $row) { echo "README.md: row already current\n"; exit(0); }
    $s = str_replace($m[0], $row . (substr($m[0], -1) === "\r" ? "\r" : ''), $s);
    file_put_contents($path, $s);
    echo "README.md: row refreshed\n"; exit(0);
}
$anchor = $eol . '| Preset engine | ';
$pos = strpos($s, $anchor);
if ($pos === false || strpos($s, $anchor, $pos + 1) !== false) { fwrite(STDERR, "anchor not found or not unique\n"); exit(2); }
$s = substr($s, 0, $pos) . $eol . $row . substr($s, $pos);
file_put_contents($path, $s);
echo "README.md: row inserted before the Preset engine row (EOL " . ($eol === "\r\n" ? 'CRLF' : 'LF') . ")\n";
